# Vault payloads are binary. `binary` is git's shorthand for `-diff -merge -text`:
# never generate a textual diff for them, never attempt a line-based merge, and
# never apply end-of-line conversion. Without this, git sniffs each blob and a
# parquet file that happens to look text-ish gets diffed byte-by-byte into the
# terminal (and, on a Windows checkout, could have its bytes rewritten by CRLF
# normalisation -- silent corruption of the archive).
*.parquet binary

# The raw NSE archives are gzip -- same reasoning.
*.json.gz binary
